---
description: How the UI talks to the API
globs: src/**/*.ts, src/**/*.tsx
alwaysApply: false
---
- Target (ADR-001): no BFF. Authenticated calls go straight from the browser to Spring Boot
  (NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL, not defined yet) with credentials: 'include'.
- Current state: auth uses Server Actions (src/features/auth/actions) + src/lib/api/http-client.ts with the
  server-only API_BASE_URL, and Next-owned HttpOnly cookies sv_at / sv_rt (src/features/auth/session).
  Keep it working; do not add new Server Actions or Route Handlers that proxy the API for new features
  unless the plan says so.
- Use the generated client in src/api/generated once it exists. Never hand-write endpoint URLs that are not
  in sunvibe-server/api/openapi.json (or the BE controllers until that file exists).
- If an endpoint is missing, STOP and write it into the hub docs/plans/<feature>-api-gaps.md.
- Public SEO pages (listing search/detail) may fetch PUBLIC endpoints in Server Components.
  Never send user tokens from the server for new code.
- Access token in memory only (auth store), sent as Authorization: Bearer. Refresh token is an
  httpOnly cookie set by the API. Never use localStorage or sessionStorage for tokens.
- API errors: use ApiError from src/lib/api; map error codes to UI messages, never show raw server text.
